  "text": "Good catch, Riley. I agree that matching the database protection limit exactly with no margin is risky. Let's set the max stale serving window at 18 minutes — that gives us a 6-minute buffer above the 12-minute recovery time you measured, and a 2-minute safety margin below the 20-minute hard ceiling. We'll document in the runbook that 20 minutes is the absolute hard ceiling from the database protection limit and that 18 minutes is our operational target to preserve margin. So the final revised policy is: (1) cache keys scoped by tenant ID plus project key, (2) security isolation test required and must pass before application sign-off, (3) fail-open mode during origin outage, (4) max stale serving window of 18 minutes with 20 minutes documented as the hard ceiling. Devon, you'll file the security finding today and give application sign-off once the isolation test passes. Riley, you'll update the runbook today with the 12-minute recovery measurement, the 20-minute database protection limit, and the 18-minute operational stale-serving target, then give reliability sign-off. If everyone agrees on this, I'm ready to settle the final policy."
}
```

